    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "WAKE ISLAND - MID PACIFIC ... a possession\nof the United States is a typical Pacific coral atoll\nconsisting of three islands, Wake Island, Wilkes\nIsland and Peale Island connected by a bridge\nand causeway... an area of two and one-half\nsquare miles formed of coral built up on an under\nwater volcano. The central lagoon is the former\ncrater and the Islands are part of the rim.\nI SDOT. 2002\nDEAR JON,\nHERE IS THE POSTCARO\nYOU REQUESTED. VISITING LAKE\nWAS A REAL TREAT. I HEPE\nYOU GET CUT THERE IN THE\nNEOR FUTURE.\nSINCERELY,\nGREG URWIN\nWake Island\nPostcard\nU^20\n3c\nUSA\n© 1993 HAWAIIAN SERVICE, INC.\nP.O. BOX 2835, HONOLULU, HAWAII 96803\nMA JON KRUPNICK\nTÓO SE 3RO AVENUE\nFI. LAUDERDALE, FLERIDA\n33316\n450071"
